  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "A bakery owner turns on his doughnut machine at \\(8\\!:\\!30\\) am. At \\(11\\!:\\!10\\) am the machine has completed one third of the day’s job. At what time will the doughnut machine complete the job?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\!:\\!50\\) pm",
    "B": "\\(3\\!:\\!00\\) pm",
    "C": "\\(3\\!:\\!30\\) pm",
    "D": "\\(4\\!:\\!30\\) pm",
    "E": "\\(5\\!:\\!50\\) pm"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "From \\(8\\!:\\!30\\) am to \\(11\\!:\\!10\\) am is \\(2\\) hours \\(40\\) minutes, or \\(160\\) minutes. At the machine's steady rate, this is one third of the total working time. Therefore the whole job takes\n\\[\n160\\div\\frac13=480\\text{ minutes}=8\\text{ hours}.\n\\]\nEight hours after \\(8\\!:\\!30\\) am is \\(\\boxed{4\\!:\\!30\\text{ pm}}\\), choice \\(\\text{D}\\).",
